I've read this argument before, but I don't get it. (I get that it's
true; I don't get why some people prefer displacement alone to
invisibility + displacement.) Displacement causes monsters attempting
to hit you miss, presumably a certain percent of the time.
Nonetheless, they can still see you, so they can still attempt to
attack you.

Monsters that can't see invisible can't see you. Not only do they
sometimes miss while trying to attack, but sometimes they simply
wander off in the wrong direction.

Is there something in the code that actually makes displacement really
more powerful than invisibility? Is the to-be-hit chance lower with
displacement than with invisibility?
